[
    {
        "content": "<p>It occasionally annoys me that <code>#synth</code> doesn't work in the middle of a proof because it won't see things in the local context for some reason:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">norm_num</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- unknown identifier G</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So I asked Claude to fix it and in under ten lines of code it claimed to do it:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- `#synth t` used *inside a tactic block* runs instance synthesis in the current local</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">context, so it sees local hypotheses and local instances (unlike the top-level `#synth`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">command, which cannot access the proof's context). Reports the instance it finds. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthLocalTac</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"#synth \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withMainContext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elabTerm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instantiateMVars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{← instantiateMVars inst} : {e}\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Diagnostic tactic: allowed to not change the goal.</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">allow_unused_tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthLocalTac</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">norm_num</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Prod.instAddCommGroup</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I don't understand a word of it but I thought I'd record it here not least because I can see myself using it later.</p>",
        "id": 609176390,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1783587950
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Something of this shape seems like worth PR'ing:)</p>",
        "id": 609194841,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Lezeau",
        "timestamp": 1783593746
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure but I have no understanding of the code and no idea if it's the right approach so definitely am not going to PR it myself; I just posted it because it's working in a simple case and might be useful for future me or other people.</p>",
        "id": 609222965,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1783602058
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The 'real' <code>#synth</code> breaks because it is a command, and commands are a syntactic category that cannot go in the middle of a <code>by</code> block; only syntax in the tactic category can go there. What Claude did is implement a tactic (so a thing in the correct syntactic category) that looks like the command. It violates the convention that syntax starting with <code>#</code> is reserved for commands. The tactic equivalent should probably be called just <code>synth</code> or <code>synth_instance</code> or something like that.</p>",
        "id": 609288466,
        "sender_full_name": "𝚠𝚘𝚓𝚌𝚒𝚎𝚌𝚑 𝚗𝚊𝚠𝚛𝚘𝚌𝚔𝚒",
        "timestamp": 1783619290
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Though we do the same thing for <code>#check</code>, which has both a tactic and command both using <code>#</code>...</p>",
        "id": 609291340,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1783620027
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Aha! Perhaps it's not as much of a convention as I thought, thanks for the correction. The reference manual says \"By convention, commands that are intended for interactive use rather than as part of a durable code artifact are prefixed with <code>#</code>.\", but it does not say this is for commands only.</p>",
        "id": 609295424,
        "sender_full_name": "𝚠𝚘𝚓𝚌𝚒𝚎𝚌𝚑 𝚗𝚊𝚠𝚛𝚘𝚌𝚔𝚒",
        "timestamp": 1783621217
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is generally true, but I think in the few situations where it makes sense to have an essentially identical tactic and command, it is nice that we make an exception for them to have the same name.</p>",
        "id": 609295716,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1783621328
    }
]